# Attributing AMT compute cost

Every job cluster AMT submits is tagged in `DatabricksExecutor._cost_tags`, so cost is a
query rather than an estimate. Cost monitor:
[dbx-cost-monitor](https://product-api-insights.dashboard.fox/pnr-exp-analyzer/dbx-cost-monitor).

| Tag | Value |
|---|---|
| `amt` | always `"true"` — every AMT cluster |
| `amt_campaign_id` | the campaign id, which is also the LangGraph thread id and MLflow experiment name |
| `amt_role` | `materialize` \| `baseline` \| `train` \| `qa0` \| `qa1` \| `final` |
| `amt_hypothesis_id` | set on `train` runs; absent on campaign-level roles |

## The query

`system.billing.usage` carries the tags and the DBU quantity; prices live separately in
`system.billing.list_prices`, so a cost in currency needs the join.

```sql
SELECT u.custom_tags['amt_campaign_id']  AS campaign,
       u.custom_tags['amt_role']         AS role,
       u.custom_tags['amt_hypothesis_id'] AS hypothesis,
       SUM(u.usage_quantity)                         AS dbus,
       SUM(u.usage_quantity * p.pricing.default)     AS usd
FROM system.billing.usage u
JOIN system.billing.list_prices p
  ON u.sku_name = p.sku_name
 AND u.usage_end_time BETWEEN p.price_start_time
                          AND coalesce(p.price_end_time, TIMESTAMP '2999-01-01')
WHERE u.custom_tags['amt'] = 'true'
  AND u.usage_date >= current_date() - INTERVAL 30 DAYS
GROUP BY ALL
ORDER BY usd DESC
```

Drop the `hypothesis` column for a per-campaign total; filter `role = 'train'` to see what
the trainer loop cost as against materialization and QA.

## What breaks attribution, in this workspace's own numbers

Tags are a property of a **job** cluster. When `AMT_EXISTING_CLUSTER_ID` pins an all-purpose
cluster, only that cluster's own static tags reach billing: a hand-added `amt=true` does keep
the cost attributable to AMT, but `amt_campaign_id`, `amt_role` and `amt_hypothesis_id` vary
per run and have nowhere to live, so all three grouping columns above go null.

Grouping the same 30 days by `sku_name` instead (measured 2026-09-17):

| SKU | Per-run tags | DBUs | USD | USD/DBU |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ENTERPRISE_ALL_PURPOSE_COMPUTE` | no | 3.14 | 2.04 | **0.650** |
| `ENTERPRISE_JOBS_COMPUTE` | yes | 10.12 | 2.02 | **0.200** |

All-Purpose is **3.25× the rate**, so the pinned cluster bought a third of the compute for the
same money — and the more expensive half is the half nothing can attribute. Prefer this
measured ratio to the "about twice" rule of thumb.

`amt doctor` reads the pinned cluster and reports this as a warning, not a failure: a warm
cluster skips the ~4.5 minutes a job cluster spends starting, which is a real trade while you
are iterating. Leave it unset for any campaign whose cost you intend to report.
